From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:48:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/55] feat(ui): the canvas's name sits quietly at the top
 left, the dock gives its room to the page

The reviewer dock opened on back, the canvas's name and its id menu:
about 300px of a bar meant for moving around and reviewing, for a name
people read once. They move to the top left (CanvasLabel), on a pill
that stays faint (surface at 70%, no ring) until the pointer or focus
comes to it, beside Present at the top right; the name truncates at
240px and is whole in its tooltip, and it is still the rename field for
those who may edit. The id menu opens downward from there.

The dock is now Hand, Comment, the zoom, the page picker and the people
menu, and the page picker's name may run to 320px (200px before). Fits
keep 52px clear at the top for the label (LABEL_CLEAR). Phones keep
their dock as it was: the name is in their canvas actions sheet.

Test: reviewerLayoutBrowser finds the label in the top-left corner,
under 340px wide, holding the id menu, and no back or id in the dock;
phoneReviewBrowser finds no label on a phone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
